---
description: Animation standards — sequential reveals, juicy feedback, intensity modes
globs:
  - "client/**"
---

- Every reveal/outcome is a **cancellable sequential timeline**:
  build tension, show the answer, punish wrong, celebrate right, then update
  standings. Never apply results in a single frame.
- Wrong answers are attacked (ships, cannons, shake, skulls, loot stolen),
  not merely dimmed. Correct answers celebrate (gold glow, sparkles, payout
  stream, ticker roll, floating text).
- Prefer Back/Bounce/Sine eases for game feel; pair squash with stretch;
  keep feedback tweens short (80-300ms) and ambient loops slow (1.5-5s).
- All new effects respect the active animation-intensity helpers and
  `prefers-reduced-motion`; reduced minimises travel/shake without removing information.
- Timelines must be cancellable (track timers, provide `cancel()`) because a
  new server state can arrive mid-animation.
- Character reactions accompany outcomes: avatars must visibly react (emote +
  squash/tint) to lock-in, loss, gain, being targeted and winning.
